 "title": "Which lattice tori make the knot unsatisfiable",
 "subject": "Satisfiability of the knot on triangular-lattice tori in every sign class",
 "conclusion": "On the lattice torus Z^2/L a sign class is satisfiable exactly when the slope triangle conv{(0,0),(p,q),(0,-r)} holds an integer point of matching parity. Hence only degenerate tori, thin tori of circumference sqrt 3 and even index (cyclic chains, solvable in O(log n) queries) and the two Fano tori have an unsatisfiable class.",
